solution:
**Given:**

If dfrac{1}{8} of a pencil is black, half of the remaining pencil is yellow and the remaining 3dfrac{1}{2} cm of the pencil is blue.

**Formula used:**

Let total length of pencil = x cm

Black part = dfrac{1}{8} x cm

Remaining length = x - dfrac{1}{8}x = dfrac{7}{8}x cm

Yellow part = dfrac{1}{2} times dfrac{7}{8}x = dfrac{7}{16}x cm

Blue part = 3dfrac{1}{2} = dfrac{7}{2} cm

**Calculation:**

x = dfrac{1}{8}x + dfrac{7}{16}x + dfrac{7}{2}

⇒ x = dfrac{2}{16}x + dfrac{7}{16}x + dfrac{7}{2}

⇒ x = dfrac{9}{16}x + dfrac{7}{2}

⇒ x - dfrac{9}{16}x = dfrac{7}{2}

⇒ dfrac{7}{16}x = dfrac{7}{2}

⇒ x = dfrac{7}{2} times dfrac{16}{7}

⇒ x = 8 cm

**∴ The correct answer is option 2.**
